    "summary": "Pristine acoustic opener and fire‑filled Scarlet > Fire sequence",
    "blurb": "The show opens with a flawless acoustic set highlighted by Bird Song before launching into an electric marathon that delivers standout Althea, Jack Straw and a classic Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain. Jerry’s lead work is consistently praised, Brent’s keyboards sparkle, and the drums drive the long second‑set jams. The superb matrix recording captures the entire performance with crystal‑clear balance.",
    "review": "On October 10, 1980 at the Warfield, the Dead delivered a show that balances delicate acoustic beauty with high‑octane electric fire. Set 1 features an immaculate acoustic segment – Bird Song glides smoothly into Ripple, and reviewers note Jerry’s “forever young” presence and Brent’s “sweet, timeless” keys. The momentum builds in Set 2 with crisp renditions of Althea, Jack Straw, and a tight Row Jimmy that keep the crowd moving.\n\nSet 3 is where the night truly ignites: a scorching Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain transition, followed by a marathon of Samson & Delilah, Estimated Prophet, and an expansive space‑driven jam that culminates in The Promised Land. Across all recordings Jerry “lays it down” with restrained yet powerful solos, Brent’s keyboards add tasteful tinkles, and both Mickey and Billy provide thick, driving rhythms that propel the third set. The matrix recording (gd1980-10-10.mtx.chappell.sb03.28740.flac16) captures this full‑show arc in excellent balance, making it the definitive listening source.",
